1
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:26,000
The game continues.

2
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:46,000
Jigsaw is a horror, mystery film directed by Michael Spierig.

3
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Law enforcement finds itself chasing the ghost of a man dead for over a
decade, embroiled in a diabolical new game that's only just begun.

4
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:26,000
John Kramer / Jigsaw, played by Tobin Bell.

5
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:46,000
Logan Nelson, played by Matt Passmore.

6
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:06,000
Detective Halloran, played by Callum Keith Rennie.

7
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Eleanor Bonneville, played by Hannah Emily Anderson.

8
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Keith Hunt, played by Clé Bennett.

9
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
Anna, played by Laura Vandervoort.

10
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:26,000
Jigsaw is a 2017 American horror film directed by the Spierig
Brothers, and written by Josh Stolberg and Peter Goldfinger.

11
00:47:40,000 --> 00:47:46,000
It is the eighth installment in the Saw film series, following Saw 3D (2010), and stars Matt Passmore, Callum Keith
Rennie, Clé Bennett, and Hannah Emily Anderson, with Tobin Bell returning to his role as John Kramer / Jigsaw.

12
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
The plot follows a group of people who find themselves forced to
participate in a series of deadly "games" inside a barn.

13
00:56:20,000 --> 00:56:26,000
Meanwhile, the police investigate a new series of murders that fit the modus operandi
of the eponymous Jigsaw Killer, who has been dead for almost a decade.

14
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
Saw 3D was deemed the final installment of the series before Lionsgate commissioned
the production of Jigsaw from a pitch by Stolberg and Goldfinger.

15
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Early development began in 2013 with production officially
starting in 2016 on a budget of $10 million.

16
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
The film was released by Lionsgate Films in the
United States on October 27, 2017.

17
01:13:40,000 --> 01:13:46,000
Jigsaw received negative reviews and grossed a
total of $104.2 million worldwide.

18
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
It was followed by a standalone installment in the series,
titled Spiral: From the Book of Saw, in 2021.

19
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:26,000
The film explores themes of sadism, gore, sequel, flashback, torture.

20
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
The tone is dark and mind_bending.
